Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A Portable Apparatus for Tracheal Insufflation Anaesthesia</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1921</year><volume>197</volume><issue>5096</issue><fpage>918</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An apparatus for the administration of nitrous oxide, oxygen, and ether</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1923</year><volume>202</volume><issue>5214</issue><fpage>228</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>KB</given-names></name></person-group><source>The development of anaesthetic apparatus: a history based on the Charles King Collection of the Association of Anaesthetists of Great Britain and Ireland</source><year>1975</year><publisher-loc>Oxford</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Blackwell Scientific Publications</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rushman</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Davies</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Atkinson</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><source>A short history of anaesthesia. The first 150 years</source><year>1996</year><publisher-loc>Oxford</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Butterworth-Heinemann</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An improved laryngoscope for anaesthetists</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1926</year><volume>207</volume><issue>5349</issue><fpage>500</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Booth</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tracheostomy and tracheal intubation in military history</article-title><source>J R Soc Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>93</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>380</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10928031</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Endotracheal anaesthesia</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>1936</year><volume>34</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>450</fpage><lpage>5</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>Section of Anaesthetics of the Royal Society of Medicine</collab><article-title>Anaesthesia in thoracic surgery</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Med</source><year>1930</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>772</fpage><lpage>82</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anaesthesia for thoracoplasty in pulmonary tuberculosis</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1930</year><volume>215</volume><issue>5554</issue><fpage>295</fpage><lpage>6</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anaesthesia in thoracic surgery, with special reference to lobectomy</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Med</source><year>1936</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>53</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>KB</given-names></name><name><surname>Sir Ivan Whiteside</surname><given-names>Magill</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>KVCO, DSc, MB, BCh, BAO, FRCS, FFARCS (Hon), FFARCSI (Hon), DA. A review of his publications and other references to his life and work</article-title><source>Anaesthesia</source><year>1978</year><volume>33</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>628</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">356665</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Warming Ether Vapour for Inhalation</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1921</year><volume>197</volume><issue>5102</issue><fpage>1270</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>Section of Anaesthetics of the Royal Society of Medicine</collab><article-title>Ethylene anaesthesia</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1930</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>862</fpage><lpage>3</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The heritages of the past are the privileges of the future</article-title><source>Anaesthesiology</source><year>1967</year><volume>28</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>202</fpage><lpage>8</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An appraisal of progress in anaesthetics</article-title><source>Ann R Coll Surg Engl</source><year>1966</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>154</fpage><lpage>65</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4952784</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boulton</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The prewar years &#x02013; 2<sup>nd</sup> July 1932 to 2<sup>nd</sup> September 1939</article-title><source>The Association of Anaesthetists of Great Britain and Ireland 1932-1992 and the development of the speciality of anaesthesia: sixty years of progress and achievement in the context of scientific, political and social change</source><year>1999</year><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Association of Anaesthetists of Great Britain and Ireland</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>KB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sir Ivan Magill: ninetieth birthday meeting</article-title><source>J R Soc Med</source><year>1979</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>71</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magill</surname><given-names>IW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modern surgical anaesthesia</article-title><source>Ulster Med J</source><year>1939</year><volume>8</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>162</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morrison</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Book review: Resuscitation greats</article-title><source>Ulster Med J</source><year>2008</year><volume>77</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>141</fpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>